-- changes, so no reset (docs/RESET.md).
--
-- - ledger_entry_type: JUDGEMENT_COMPENSATION ('판정 오류 보상'), a mint into the compensated
--   member's user ledger account naming the market it compensates, appended with ADD VALUE — so
--   nothing in this batch names it as the enum (55P04, migrations 0014, 0043, 0077): the
--   functions compare text, and the triggers below compare `type::text` in a WHEN and in bodies
--   that run after the batch commits.
-- - judgement_compensations: one row per account an approved `market_judgement_compensation`
--   request listed, written whole by `payJudgementCompensation` (@buddha/db) in the approving
--   transaction at the decision's instant and never changed: the confirmed incident and its
--   market, the account, what the correction owes it (recomputed here from its settlement records,
